  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Tuesday/... \nDuring the weekend, some semblance of a Rex block (or omega block) \nwill develop in the southern stream with weak troughing over \nnorthern Mexico and broad ridging across the Great Basin/central \nRockies. While the precise orientation and positioning of salient \nfeatures remain uncertain based on notable ensemble differences, the \noverall pattern will promote surface pressure rises over the \nintermountain West and dry N/NE boundary layer flow. Based on the \npattern, periods of breezy northeast winds are likely at times over \nthe weekend and early next week, though nothing particularly strong \nor unusual for this time of year. At some point early next week, the \nbulk of ensemble members eject the northern Mexico wave through the \nforecast area bringing enhanced mid/upper level moisture. It remains \nto be seen whether this process can overcome the dry boundary layer \nairmass, with the highest odds suggesting dry weather persisting. \nWith H5 heights remaining nearly steady state in a 580-584dm range, \ntemperatures should follow a near persistence trends with readings \nnot terribly far from climatology.",
